\ Third Genstat reference program for predictmeans: variance components and
\ their s.e. for varcomp(), with edge cases. Please save the whole Output
\ window (File > Save) and send that file; the first run may need small
\ syntax fixes. Cases: (1) Dyestuff, random Batch; (2) Dyestuff2, the Batch
\ variance estimated at zero (Genstat may report a bound or a negative value);
\ (3) Penicillin, crossed random plate and sample; (4) Orthodont, random
\ intercept and uncorrelated random slope of age; (5) Orthodont, random
\ intercept with AR(1) between the four ages of each child.

\ ---- 1 and 2. Dyestuff and Dyestuff2 (6 batches x 5) ----
UNITS [NVALUES=30]
FACTOR [LEVELS=6] Batch
VARIATE Yield, Yield2
READ Batch, Yield, Yield2
1 1545 7.298   1 1440 3.846   1 1440 2.434   1 1520 9.566   1 1580 7.99   2 1540 5.22
2 1555 6.556   2 1490 0.608   2 1560 11.788   2 1495 -0.892   3 1595 0.11   3 1550 10.386
3 1605 13.434   3 1510 5.51   3 1560 8.166   4 1445 2.212   4 1440 4.852   4 1595 7.092
4 1465 9.288   4 1545 4.98   5 1595 0.282   5 1630 9.014   5 1515 4.458   5 1635 9.446
5 1625 7.198   6 1520 1.722   6 1455 4.782   6 1450 8.106   6 1480 0.758   6 1445 3.758
:
VCOMPONENTS RANDOM=Batch
REML [PRINT=model, components; METHOD=AI] Yield
REML [PRINT=model, components; METHOD=AI] Yield2

\ ---- 3. Penicillin: 24 plates x 6 samples, crossed ----
UNITS [NVALUES=144]
FACTOR [LEVELS=24] plate
FACTOR [LEVELS=6] sample
VARIATE diameter
READ plate, sample, diameter
1 1 27   1 2 23   1 3 26   1 4 23   1 5 23   1 6 21
2 1 27   2 2 23   2 3 26   2 4 23   2 5 23   2 6 21
3 1 25   3 2 21   3 3 25   3 4 24   3 5 24   3 6 20
4 1 26   4 2 23   4 3 25   4 4 23   4 5 23   4 6 20
5 1 25   5 2 22   5 3 26   5 4 22   5 5 23   5 6 20
6 1 24   6 2 22   6 3 25   6 4 23   6 5 22   6 6 19
7 1 24   7 2 20   7 3 23   7 4 21   7 5 22   7 6 19
8 1 26   8 2 22   8 3 26   8 4 24   8 5 24   8 6 21
9 1 24   9 2 21   9 3 24   9 4 22   9 5 22   9 6 20
10 1 24   10 2 21   10 3 24   10 4 23   10 5 22   10 6 19
11 1 26   11 2 23   11 3 26   11 4 24   11 5 24   11 6 21
12 1 25   12 2 22   12 3 26   12 4 24   12 5 24   12 6 20
13 1 26   13 2 24   13 3 26   13 4 24   13 5 25   13 6 22
14 1 26   14 2 23   14 3 26   14 4 23   14 5 23   14 6 20
15 1 26   15 2 23   15 3 25   15 4 24   15 5 24   15 6 22
16 1 25   16 2 22   16 3 25   16 4 23   16 5 23   16 6 20
17 1 25   17 2 21   17 3 24   17 4 23   17 5 23   17 6 20
18 1 25   18 2 22   18 3 24   18 4 23   18 5 23   18 6 19
19 1 24   19 2 21   19 3 23   19 4 21   19 5 21   19 6 19
20 1 26   20 2 23   20 3 26   20 4 24   20 5 24   20 6 21
21 1 25   21 2 21   21 3 24   21 4 22   21 5 22   21 6 18
22 1 25   22 2 22   22 3 25   22 4 22   22 5 22   22 6 20
23 1 24   23 2 21   23 3 24   23 4 22   23 5 24   23 6 19
24 1 24   24 2 21   24 3 24   24 4 22   24 5 21   24 6 18
:
VCOMPONENTS RANDOM=plate + sample
REML [PRINT=model, components; METHOD=AI] diameter

\ ---- 4 and 5. Orthodont: 27 children x 4 ages (8, 10, 12, 14) ----
UNITS [NVALUES=108]
FACTOR [LEVELS=27] Subject
FACTOR [LEVELS=4] Occ
VARIATE age, distance
READ Subject, Occ, age, distance
1 1 8 26   1 2 10 25   1 3 12 29   1 4 14 31
2 1 8 21.5   2 2 10 22.5   2 3 12 23   2 4 14 26.5
3 1 8 23   3 2 10 22.5   3 3 12 24   3 4 14 27.5
4 1 8 25.5   4 2 10 27.5   4 3 12 26.5   4 4 14 27
5 1 8 20   5 2 10 23.5   5 3 12 22.5   5 4 14 26
6 1 8 24.5   6 2 10 25.5   6 3 12 27   6 4 14 28.5
7 1 8 22   7 2 10 22   7 3 12 24.5   7 4 14 26.5
8 1 8 24   8 2 10 21.5   8 3 12 24.5   8 4 14 25.5
9 1 8 23   9 2 10 20.5   9 3 12 31   9 4 14 26
10 1 8 27.5   10 2 10 28   10 3 12 31   10 4 14 31.5
11 1 8 23   11 2 10 23   11 3 12 23.5   11 4 14 25
12 1 8 21.5   12 2 10 23.5   12 3 12 24   12 4 14 28
13 1 8 17   13 2 10 24.5   13 3 12 26   13 4 14 29.5
14 1 8 22.5   14 2 10 25.5   14 3 12 25.5   14 4 14 26
15 1 8 23   15 2 10 24.5   15 3 12 26   15 4 14 30
16 1 8 22   16 2 10 21.5   16 3 12 23.5   16 4 14 25
17 1 8 21   17 2 10 20   17 3 12 21.5   17 4 14 23
18 1 8 21   18 2 10 21.5   18 3 12 24   18 4 14 25.5
19 1 8 20.5   19 2 10 24   19 3 12 24.5   19 4 14 26
20 1 8 23.5   20 2 10 24.5   20 3 12 25   20 4 14 26.5
21 1 8 21.5   21 2 10 23   21 3 12 22.5   21 4 14 23.5
22 1 8 20   22 2 10 21   22 3 12 21   22 4 14 22.5
23 1 8 21.5   23 2 10 22.5   23 3 12 23   23 4 14 25
24 1 8 23   24 2 10 23   24 3 12 23.5   24 4 14 24
25 1 8 20   25 2 10 21   25 3 12 22   25 4 14 21.5
26 1 8 16.5   26 2 10 19   26 3 12 19   26 4 14 19.5
27 1 8 24.5   27 2 10 25   27 3 12 28   27 4 14 28
:
\ (4) random intercept and an uncorrelated random slope (lmer: age || Subject)
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=age] RANDOM=Subject + Subject.age
REML [PRINT=model, components; METHOD=AI] distance
\ (5) random intercept; AR(1) between the ages of each child in the residual
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=age] RANDOM=Subject + Subject.Occ
VSTRUCTURE [TERMS=Subject.Occ] FACTOR=Occ; MODEL=AR; ORDER=1
REML [PRINT=model, components; METHOD=AI] distance
STOP
